    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d989">

                <pb facs="1134" n="1022" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg1022"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611B.9417/102a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Department of State to the Japanese
                        Embassy</hi><anchor n="97" xml:id="d989-f1"/></head>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Philippine customs statistics indicate that imports of Japanese cotton
                        piece goods into the Philippines during the first three months of the
                        agreement, August, September and October, totaled 26,021,000 square
                        meters.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Reports from the Philippine customs service indicate that the liquidation
                        of duty on Japanese cotton piece goods has continued in November so that the
                        statistics for November will show imports for the first four months of the
                        agreement several million square meters in excess of the agreed maximum for
                        any six months’ period.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>The Philippine customs service reports that arrivals of Japanese goods in
                        November continue heavy, arrivals during the first half of the month
                        totaling 4,000 packages, a slightly higher rate than during the previous
                        three months.</item>
                    <pb facs="1135" n="1023" xml:id="pg1023"/>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>It is probable that there is a sufficient amount of Japanese cotton goods
                        already in the Philippines to produce a total figure of imports of Japanese
                        cotton piece goods during the first six or eight months of the agreement
                        twice as great as the maximum agreed upon for any six months’ period.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">[<placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1935-11-27">November 27,
                            1935</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d989-f1" n="97" type="source" xml:id="d989-f1-content">
